      "side": 1,
      "message": "It does!\n\nIn https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/4556450 I changed this script to use binutils provided by our toolchain, e.g `armv7m-cros-eabi-objdump` as I thought it would be the best option.\n\nFor me, the problem is that `armv7m-cros-eabi` toolchain provides tools that are incompatible.\n\nLLVM is a native cross compiler (which means that one executable can generate code for multiple architectures). This has a huge advantage that we can use standard LLVM binutils. This patch also makes our codebase more aligned with Zephyr which is always good :)",
